# Loop variable does not escape the loop

Verifies the `for` range loop variable lives only inside the loop body. Reading
it after the loop fails with the standard unknown-binding diagnostic.

>>> source
for (item in 0..3) {
    print(item)
}

print(item)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: unknown binding `item` at Span { start: 46, end: 50 }

<<< exit
1
